ms. The only way to learn the actual counts is to run the exact recurrence, in code, and tally the results."}],"mechanism":"The LCG X_(n+1) = (1103515245 * X_n + 12345) mod 2^31 is iterated exactly using Python big integers with X_0=42. For each n from 1 to 10000, die_n = 1 + (X_n mod 6). Tally counts[face] across 10000 draws, return count_1..count_6 and total as flat observables, and include calibration_0..calibration_9 as the first ten (x_n, die_n) pairs so the recurrence can be verified by hand.","optional_refs":["src-a242c7242fff06a281ecdccb74d052ae9e9c0e9b","f3ecc13577e847a30232d29efd36717534322216333c3912f1ed39b5e7442762"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.97}],"simulation_proposals":[{"declared_assumptions":["Python's % operator on non-negative big integers is equivalent to the mathematical modulo operation.","The recurrence and face-mapping are exactly as specified in the problem statement.","n=1 corresponds to X_1 (after one LCG step), not X_0=42.","The requested observables must be flat single-segment identifiers as required by the schema.","Integer arithmetic only; no floats; no imports needed.","The simulation function carries everything internally; rng is unused because the LCG is deterministic from X_0=42."],"discriminating_purpose":"Return the exact six face counts and a ten-step calibration trace for the specified LCG over 10000 draws so the fairness verdict can be adjudicated externally from raw data.","hypothesis":"The exact face-count distribution of the LCG sequence X_0=42, X_(n+1) = (1103515245 * X_n + 12345) mod 2^31, die_n = 1 + (X_n mod 6), for n=1..10000, can be obtained by running the exact integer recurrence in Python and tallying. The calibration trace (first ten X_n, die_n pairs) should match hand computation.","input_aliases":[],"interpretation_conditions":["calibration_0 through calibration_9 should be the X_n values for n=1..10; they can be hand-verified from X_0=42.","calibration_d